# Ingore MacOS files
.DS_Store
.vscode
Bramble.code-workspace

# Files generated by invoking Julia with --code-coverage
*.jl.cov
*.jl.*.cov
*.csv

# Files generated by invoking Julia with --track-allocation
*.jl.mem

# System-specific files and directories generated by the BinaryProvider and BinDeps packages
# They contain absolute paths specific to the host computer, and so should not be committed
deps/deps.jl
deps/build.log
deps/downloads/
deps/usr/
deps/src/

# Build artifacts for creating documentation generated by the Documenter package
docs/build/
docs/site/

# LaTeX build artifacts from the manual. Scoped to manual/ rather than global, so a .tex
# file kept deliberately elsewhere — a figure source, say — is unaffected.
#
# The sources are manual/*.tex, manual/chapters/, manual/preamble.tex, manual/assets/ and
# build.sh; everything below is regenerated by running it.
manual/*.aux
manual/*.bbl
manual/*.blg
manual/*.fdb_latexmk
manual/*.fls
manual/*.idx
manual/*.ilg
manual/*.ind
manual/*.lof
manual/*.log
manual/*.lot
manual/*.nav
manual/*.out
manual/*.snm
manual/*.synctex.gz
manual/*.toc
manual/*.vrb
manual/chapters/*.aux

# The rendered manual and its preview image. Regenerated by build.sh, and a PDF churns the
# whole binary on every rebuild, so it is kept out rather than versioned. If the built
# manual should ship with the repository instead, drop these two lines and commit it — but
# prefer attaching it to a release, where a large binary does not enter every clone.
manual/*.pdf
manual/*.pdf.png

# OneDrive sync conflicts. The repository lives inside a OneDrive folder, and when the
# same path is written on two machines OneDrive keeps both by appending a space and a
# number to the name: `docs/build 2/`, `assets 2/`, and so on. They are duplicates of
# ignored build output but the ignore rules above do not match the renamed form, so
# `git add -A` would commit them.
*\ [0-9]
*\ [0-9]/
*\ [0-9].*
*\ [0-9][0-9]
*\ [0-9][0-9]/
*\ [0-9][0-9].*

# File generated by Pkg, the package manager, based on a corresponding Project.toml
# It records a fixed state of all packages used by the project. As such, it should not be
# committed for packages, but should be committed for applications that require a static
# environment.
Manifest.toml
*.mp4

# other stuff
# Scratch benchmarking stays ignored, but the committed regression suite does not: an
# uncommitted benchmark suite cannot be a baseline for anyone else. The directory is
# excluded by its contents rather than as a whole, since git does not descend into an
# excluded directory and the negations below would never be reached.
benchmark/*
!benchmark/benchmarks.jl
!benchmark/Project.toml
!benchmark/baselines/
!benchmark/baselines/*.json
playground/
build/
research/
test_code_warntype/
.agents/
.claude/
LocalPreferences.toml
AGENTS.md
polygonal_mesh_plan.md

# The manual is written and built outside version control, by request.
# This covers its sources, its LaTeX build products and the design preview.
manual/
docs/manual_design_preview.html

# Working notes for the form-layer unlock, paired with the tracker artifact. Kept out of
# version control by request: the history and the open questions live here, not on GitHub.
docs/form-unlock-plan.md
